\ `SeqInt` and `SeqBool` are how the target spells `Seq Int` and `Seq Bool`.
\ Neither is a source type, so the checker refuses `SeqInt` here as it would
\ any other name that is not a type (`dec.source-type-names`). The compiler
\ keeps its own guard: a word over an opaque `SeqInt` and one over `Seq Int`
\ would otherwise compile to the same type.
: keep
  (forall ρ; ρ x:SeqInt^many -- ρ x:SeqInt^many)
  ;

: reserved-type-name ( -- ) ;
